📜 🔤../shared/bytes.🍇🔤

💭 The eight numbers a digest is made of, and the work of mixing a block into them
💭 (FIPS 180-4, 6.2.2). It is an object because a list is a value here: a routine that
💭 is handed one gets a copy, and cannot fill the caller's.
💭
💭 Numbers have 64 bits and the algorithm's have 32, so every sum is cut back to 32
💭 bits, and so is every turn: a turn to the right is a shift each way, and the shift
💭 to the left leaves bits above the 32.
